.TH NETMAIL 8N UniSoft
.SH NAME
netmail \- the bnet network mail system
.SH DESCRIPTION
The bnet network mail system 
consists of the following
programs:
.TP .3i
.B /etc/bnetmaild
a simple mail daemon run by crontab or by hand.  Looks in the
.I "mail spool directory\^"
.RB ( /usr/spool/netmail ) 
for files to send out onto the network.  Uses
.I remsh\^
to send mail to remote hosts.  
Deletes mail if the mail is apparently successfully sent.  
Deletes mail found lying around which is more than one week old; apparently
the destination host in this case is off the net.  
Accepts no arguments.
.TP
.B /etc/delivermail
.IR exec\^ 'd 
by 
.B /bin/mail
to deliver mail to users or networks depending on the 
contents of the address of the mail.  
If the address contains an
.RS .3i
.TP .3i
\fB@\fR
then deliver to the bnet network, else if the address has a
.TP
.B ! 
then deliver to the uucp network,
.TP .3i
.BI " "
else deliver locally.
.RE
.TP .3i
.B /etc/netmailer
.IR exec\^ 'd 
by 
.B /etc/delivermail
to "deliver" netmail.  Mail is actually deposited in 
.B /usr/spool/netmail
with appropriate network mail headers prepended.  
.B /etc/bnetmaild
actually sends the mail to the network.  See
.IR netmailer\^ (8N)
for a description of flag arguments.
.TP
.B /bin/mail
has been modified to 
.I exec\^
.B /etc/delivermail
.RI ( delivermail\^ (8N))
which does aliasing and re-routing of mail destined for the b-network.
.SH FILES
.TP .3i
/usr/spool/netmail
directory for network mail
.TP
/usr/spool/netmail/bnetXXXXXX
actual mail file(s), XXXXXX = pid.
.SH SEE ALSO
mail(1), remsh(1N), delivermail(8N), netmailer(8N).
.SH BUGS
.PP
Many, no doubt; for example, lots of work should be done on 
.BR /etc/bnetmaild ,
i.e., if a piece of mail is
deleted due to its being old or otherwise undeliverable, notification should
be sent to the originator.  Soon, however, 
.I bnetmaild 
will be replaced by 
.IR sendmail .
.PP
A front-end is needed for mail, such as 
.I Mail 
(ucb).
.\"	 @(#)netmail.8n	 5.2 of 7/26/84
